				142,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Sky): Add diagnostic logging to webview postMessage bridge\n\nInstrument the `sky://webview/postMessage` handler in `Bridge.ts` to log key lifecycle events to the Mountain diagnostic channel. Insert `MountainIPCInvoke` calls to capture: entry receipt, registry lookup state, successful dispatch attempt, and execution errors.\n\nThese logs include the ViewId, message type availability, and registry status to facilitate debugging of IPC failures between the Astro UI and the VS Code workbench webviews. Error messages are truncated to 120 characters to fit diagnostic buffers.\n\nThis enhancement provides visibility into the event bridge's internal flow without altering the core dispatch logic or payload structure.",
			"SHA": "0a8df619b8456c80cf6b1a1de951bf8512caadf5"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-16T00:02:46Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				142,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Sky): Standardize emoji spacing in architecture documentation\n\nAlign the `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` file with the project's style guide by ensuring consistent spacing between section titles and their corresponding emojis. The previous format used non-breaking spaces or inconsistent whitespace which disrupted the visual flow in markdown renderers. Update all section headers (Overview, Architecture, Module Map, etc.) to use a single standard space character before the emoji icon.\n\nThis change maintains the integrity of the visual navigation aids while ensuring compatibility with standard markdown parsers and documentation viewers.",
			"SHA": "e76082c1521bc37361588b2df8d70aa9cf435cb5"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T23:36:25Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				142,
				2
			],
			"Message": "docs(Sky): Standardize markdown formatting and update related links\n\nRefactor `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` to improve readability by converting paragraphs into bullet lists, adding section emojis, and updating relative links to full GitHub URLs for external component documentation. This ensures consistency with the project's documentation style guide.\n\nSimultaneously, refactor `Source/Function/Sky/Bridge.ts` to strictly access object properties on the `Wire` DTO using bracket notation (e.g., `Wire[\"handle\"]`) instead of dot notation. This change enforces robust handling of dynamic keys in the Tauri IPC payload and aligns with the strict TypeScript configuration for the Sky component layer.\n\nThese updates clarify the architectural separation between the Astro UI and the backend while improving the robustness of the event bridge implementation.",
			"SHA": "d48d55cef3bc57e37ad3ff79cbc382d7a5b71485"
		}
	],
